ection as the only self-consistent answer. I'm now weighing whether the differing inputs might still make the two functions provably agree, but the essay's own example treats different-observation copies as separate nodes, so I'll follow that.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working under the A-FDT reading: intervening on Sasha's input, while the other copy runs a different input, so I'm checking whether the two are subjunctively linked. I'm also asking whether the other copy's prior should match the FDT output at its own input, and that symmetry question is where I'm stuck.\n\nUnder A-FDT the other copy's node is held at its prior, so with defection dominating for a fixed other, I'm getting mutual defection as the only self-consistent answer. I'm now weighing whether the differing inputs might still make the two functions provably agree, but the essay's own example treats different-observation copies as separate nodes, so I'll follow that.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9847,"completion_tokens":917,"total_tokens":10764,"cost":0.057728,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.057728,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039388,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01834},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":500,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}